  "report_fragments": [
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0001",
      "text": "veNFT can be transferred to address(0), permanently losing locked HYBR tokens"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0002",
      "text": "The `VotingEscrow` contract allows veNFTs to be transferred to `address(0)`, which permanently locks the underlying HYBR tokens. The documentation says it should revert, but the code doesn't check for zero address."
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0003",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0004",
      "text": "## Vulnerability Details"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0005",
      "text": "### The Bug"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0006",
      "text": "The `_transferFrom` function doesn't check if the recipient is `address(0)`. The documentation says it should revert, but it doesn't."
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0007",
      "text": "**Vulnerable Code**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0008",
      "text": "**What happens when transferred to address(0)**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0009",
      "text": "- veNFT ownership goes to `address(0)`"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0010",
      "text": "- Locked HYBR stays in contract"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0011",
      "text": "- No one can withdraw it"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0012",
      "text": "- Tokens are lost forever"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0013",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0014",
      "text": "## How This Can Happen"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0015",
      "text": "**User makes typo**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0016",
      "text": "- Wants to send to: `0x1234...5678`"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0017",
      "text": "- Types: `0x0000...0000` (address(0))"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0018",
      "text": "- veNFT goes to address(0), HYBR locked forever"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0019",
      "text": "**Contract bug**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0020",
      "text": "- Integration contract has uninitialized address"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0021",
      "text": "- Calls `transferFrom(user, address(0), tokenId)`"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0022",
      "text": "- User loses veNFT and locked HYBR"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0023",
      "text": "**Malicious operator**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0024",
      "text": "- User approved operator for convenience"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0025",
      "text": "- Operator transfers to address(0)"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0026",
      "text": "- User's funds stolen"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0027",
      "text": "Evidence"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0028",
      "text": "**1. Documentation says it should check**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0029",
      "text": "**2. ERC721 standard requires it**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0030",
      "text": "- EIP-721 says: \"Throws if `_to` is the zero address\""
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0031",
      "text": "- This is mandatory for ERC721 compliance"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0032",
      "text": "**3. Other contracts in codebase have this check**:"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0033",
      "text": "- CLFactory: `require(token0 != address(0))`"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0034",
      "text": "- GaugeManager: `require(tokenA != address(0))`"
    },
    {
      "id": "e_b9bd782e2132_0035",
      "text": "- But VotingEscrow doesn't"
    }
  ]
}
